  "generated_text": "1. We know that in a right triangle, the side opposite the $30^\\circ$ angle is half the length of the hypotenuse.\n2. Let's denote the hypotenuse by \\( c \\).\n3. According to the problem, the leg opposite the $30^\\circ$ angle is 12 inches.\n4. Therefore, we can write the equation:\n   \\[\n   \\frac{1}{2}c = 12\n   \\]\n5. To find \\( c \\), we multiply both sides of the equation by 2:\n   \\[\n   c = 12 \\times 2\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   c = 24\n   \\]\n\nSo, the length of the hypotenuse is \\(\\boxed{24}\\) inches.",
  "grade": {
    "error": null,
    "extracted_answer": "[24, '24']",
    "gold_answer": "A right triangle with a $30^\\circ$ angle is a 30-60-90 triangle.  In such a triangle, the hypotenuse has twice the length of the leg opposite the $30^\\circ$ angle, so the hypotenuse of the triangle in the problem has length $2\\cdot 12 = \\boxed{24}$ inches.",
    "is_correct": true
  },
